      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I see what you did there with the bolding and the phrasing. It's getting a bit repetitive, though.\n\nCan you rewrite the whole section with a full breakdown of all the phases (prophase, metaphase, anaphase, telophase, and cytokinesis)? I need the actual science to be much more thorough. \n\nAlso, the ranking tool is still flagging this as \"low engagement\" because of the word count for those specific terms. I'm telling you, don't make it weird or robotic, but it definitely needs to use those \"helpful/understand/learn\" terms more frequently to hit the threshold for a \"high-quality instruction\" flag in our system. Just try to weave them in naturally while you explain the actual biology. Thanks!",
